    "mechanism": "质谱检测ApoE亚型特异性肽段，推断APOE ε4携带状态并反映ApoE代谢",
    "status": "高度验证/即将临床",
    "sample": "血浆",
    "finding": "【核心证据】C2N团队研究显示：整合血浆Aβ42/40比值、ApoE蛋白型与年龄的检测模型可准确识别脑淀粉样阳性个体（Molecular Neurodegeneration 2021，DOI 10.1186/s13024-021-00451-6）；配套LC-MS/MS方法学验证见Clin Chim Acta 2021（DOI 10.1016/j.cca.2021.05.011）。【价值】ApoE蛋白型由质谱检测ApoE亚型特异性肽段推断，可在不测基因型的情况下获得APOE ε4状态信息。｜【证据1·Molecular neurodegeneration 2021】(PMID 33933117) We used receiver operating characteristic curve (ROC) analyses to assess assay performance and accuracy for predicting amyloid status (positive, negative, and standard uptake value ratio; SUVR). The AUC-ROC (0.86; 95% CI = 0.82-0.90) and accuracy (81%) for the plasma Aβ42/40 ratio improved after controlling for cohort heterogeneity.｜【证据2·Clinica chimica acta; international journal of clinical chemistry 2021】(PMID 34015303) In accord with CLIA standards, we developed and validated assay performance: precision, accuracy, linearity, limit of detection (LoD), interferences. APOE proteotypes were 100% concordant with genotype, while LoD (fM) was much lower than APOE concentrations observed in plasma (mM).｜【证据3·Journal of investigative medicine : the official publication of the American Federation for Clinical Research 2024】(PMID 38548482) In addition, variants of the apolipoprotein E (APOE) gene are associated with variable AD risk. Beta-amyloid (Aβ) plays an important role in AD pathology, and the Aβ42/40 peptide ratio is a good indicator for amyloid deposition.",
