    "status": "高度验证/即将临床",
    "sample": "CSF/血浆",
    "finding": "【证据1·Molecular & cellular proteomics : MCP 2023】(PMID 37024090) Multiplex tandem mass tag MS (TMT-MS) proteomic data (n = 7787 proteins) was generated on brain tissue from Brodmann area 6 and Brodmann area 37 (n = 109 cases, n = 218 total samples) and evaluated by consensus weighted gene correlation network analysis. To better understand the molecular mechanisms of resilience to Aβ provided by NRN1, we assessed how exogenous NRN1 alters the proteome by TMT-MS (n = 8238 proteins) of cultured neurons and integrated the results with the AD brain network.｜【证据2·Alzheimer's & dementia : the journal of the Alzheimer's Association 2026】(PMID 41645874) Neuritin-1 (NRN1) was identified as a synaptic protein associated with cognitive resilience to Alzheimer's disease (AD). Based on single-nucleus RNA sequencing from SEA-AD, NRN1 expression in excitatory neurons tends to decrease with increasing donor pseudo-progression.｜【证据3·International journal of molecular medicine 2020】(PMID 32626916) In the present study, it was found that miR‑199a decreased Neuritin expression and was therefore involved in the development of AD. Subsequently, differentially expressed miRNAs in AD from datasets and the literature were recruited, and those that could bind Neuritin were predicted using bioinformatics analysis.",
