    "mechanism": "晚发型AD最强遗传风险因素，影响Aβ清除、脂质代谢、小胶质反应与突触修复",
    "status": "科研探索",
    "sample": "血液/唾液",
    "finding": "【核心证据】APOE ε4是晚发型AD最强的遗传风险因素，除影响Aβ清除外，还与小胶质反应改变、脂质代谢失调、炎症信号增强、突触修复受损及神经元易感性增加相关。【临床定位】主要用于风险分层与临床试验入组，不单独作为诊断标志物；与血浆Aβ42/40、GFAP、年龄联合可显著提高淀粉样PET阳性的识别准确率。｜【证据1·Science translational medicine 2024】(PMID 38924431) Here, we characterized the proteomic landscape of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) changes associated with Aβ and tau pathology in 300 individuals using two different proteomic technologies-tandem mass tag mass spectrometry and SomaScan. Integration of both data types allowed for generation of a robust protein coexpression network consisting of 34 modules derived from 5242 protein measurements, including disease-relevant modules associated with autophagy, ubiquitination, endocytosis, and glycolysis.｜【证据2·Journal of Alzheimer's disease : JAD 2025】(PMID 40692324) Subgroup analyses were performed by baseline tau burden and APOE ε4 genotype.ResultsThree trials (n = 2054) were included. Donanemab modestly reduced cognitive decline compared to placebo: ADAS-Cog13 (MD, -1.86), CDR-SB (MD, -0.36), MMSE (MD, 0.64), and iADRS (MD, 3.19), with similar effects across tau subgroups.｜【证据3·European journal of medical research 2025】(PMID 40660381) Pathological mechanisms and treatment progression of Alzheimer's disease",
