    "mechanism": "TDP-43功能丧失导致HDGFL2隐蔽外显子表达，可作为LATE/AD共病理的血液标志物",
    "status": "科研探索",
    "sample": "CSF/血浆",
    "finding": "【机制】TDP-43功能丧失导致HDGFL2等基因产生隐蔽外显子（cryptic exon）编码的新型蛋白，可作为TDP-43病理的体液标志物。【核心证据】研究显示HDGFL2隐蔽蛋白可报告神经退行性疾病中的TDP-43病理存在（Molecular Neurodegeneration 2024，DOI 10.1186/s13024-024-00718-8）；TDP-43剪接抑制丧失在老年人群中早期出现并与病理相关（Acta Neuropathologica 2023，DOI 10.1007/s00401-023-02653-2）。｜【证据1·Nature medicine 2024】(PMID 38890531) Plasma EV TDP-43 levels and EV 3R/4R tau ratios were determined in a cohort of 704 patients, including 37 genetically and 31 neuropathologically proven cases. Both markers discriminated between the diagnostic groups with area under the curve values >0.9, and between TDP-43 and tau pathology in bvFTD.｜【证据2·Molecular neurodegeneration 2025】(PMID 41233885) Plasma TDP-43 is a potential biomarker for advanced limbic-predominant age-related TDP-43 encephalopathy neuropathologic change｜【证据3·Scientific reports 2024】(PMID 39294194) Novel TDP-43 immunoassays were developed on three different technical platforms and qualified for specificity, signal-to-noise ratio, detection range, variation, spike recovery and dilution linearity in human plasma samples. Surprisingly, implementation of these assays demonstrated that biobank-archived plasma samples yielded considerable heterogeneity in TDP-43 levels.",
