    "sample": "CSF/皮肤/血浆",
    "finding": "【核心证据】α-突触核蛋白种子扩增检测（SAA/RT-QuIC）可在CSF中识别路易体共病理：在常染色体显性AD队列中检出路易体共病理（Alzheimers Dement TRCI 2024，DOI 10.1002/alz.13818）；在散发性AD队列中，SAA阳性与疾病进展加速和认知下降相关（DOI 10.1002/alz.14276）。【边界】SAA阳性并不局限于突触核蛋白病，在部分非突触核蛋白病中亦可阳性（EBioMedicine 2025，DOI 10.1016/j.ebiom.2025.105925），解读需结合临床。｜【证据1·Alzheimer's & dementia : the journal of the Alzheimer's Association 2024】(PMID 39428831) SAA+ conversion was associated with CSF Aβ42 positivity but did not impact the progression of either CSF Aβ42 or CSF p-tau181 status. CSF Aβ42, p-tau181, and α-syn SAA were all strong predictors of clinical progression, particularly CSF Aβ42.｜【证据2·Alzheimer's & dementia : the journal of the Alzheimer's Association 2024】(PMID 38666355) Results suggest that in ADAD LBP occurs later than AD pathology and often as amygdala- or olfactory-predominant LBP, for which CSF α-synuclein SAA has low sensitivity. CSF α-synuclein RT-QuIC has low sensitivity for focal, low-burden LBP.｜【证据3·Alzheimer's & dementia : the journal of the Alzheimer's Association 2024】(PMID 38323747) The prevalence and clinical impact of CSF αS-SAA positivity in AD are still unknown. αS-SAA was performed on CSF samples from 240 AD patients (preclinical, prodromal, and dementia stages), 85 controls, 84 patients with Parkinson's disease (PD), and 21 patients with PD with dementia or dementia wi… In AD patients, associations between αS-SAA positivity and cognitive changes were also evaluated.",
